      "question": {
        "math_academy_id": "q-124301",
        "knowledge_point_id": "dd51cf5a-ca8a-5f89-91d6-8f1a58412314",
        "knowledge_point": "Finding the Matrix Representation of an Affine Transformation Given its Parametric Form",
        "problem": "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx=6u-v,\\,y=2u-3v+4\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}a & -1 \\\\ 2 & b\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ c\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
        "worked_solution": "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nFirst, notice that we can express the given transformation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}6u-v \\\\ 2u-3v+4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSeparating the constants and expressing the linear part as a product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}6u-v \\\\ 2u-3v+4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}6u-v \\\\ 2u-3v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}6 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=6+(-3)+4=7.\n$$",
        "answer_fields": [
          {
            "key": "selection",
            "type": "radio",
            "choices_complete": true,
