        "worked_solution": "The given operator is a third-order differential operator of the form\n\n$$\nD(y)={f}_{3}(x,y)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}+{f}_{2}(x,y)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x,y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x,y)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{3}=xy,{f}_{2}=0,{f}_{1}=0,$ and ${f}_{0}=3.$\n\nTo compute $D(y),$ we apply the definition of the operator $D$ to the function $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D(\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x) & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\cdot (-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x(3-8x\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        "answer_fields": [
